From d71cf8d0359085c8ca0fcc4ca3df80b0b0b66538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:52:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] Per-client presence + focus model for live session
 tracking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the prior per-session SSE refcount mechanism (the original
0009 + ~10 follow-up patches) with a single-connection-per-client
presence model.

Each TUI process opens ONE long-lived SSE on `/event` with header
`X-Client-ID: <uuid>`. The connection itself is the presence beacon;
when it closes, `stream.onAbort` fires once and the entry is removed.
Focus changes within the TUI are signaled out-of-band via
`POST /event/focus { sessionID | null }`.

Why this fixes the leak class the prior patches kept chasing:

  - One connection per TUI instead of one per session-view → cleanup
    runs once when the TUI dies, not per navigation. Far fewer paths
    to leak.
  - `stream.onAbort` is registered BEFORE `_clients.set`. There is no
    "_incr ran but listener wasn't installed yet" race window. If
    `stream.aborted` is true at registration time, we bail
    synchronously before any state mutation.
  - On Bun >= 1.2 the canonical disconnect signal is the
    ReadableStream cancel → stream.abort path that drives onAbort
    listeners. The prior code's reliance on `c.req.raw.signal` was a
    legacy-Bun fallback that no longer fires; the prior `Connection:
    close` header was fighting Hono's `keep-alive` default and not
    helping.
  - Focus is explicit server-side state, not derived from request
    query params. The same connection can rebind focus any number of
    times without churning sockets.

`expandedLiveSet()` semantics carry over: `sessions = focused ∪
direct children of focused roots`, `subagents = subagent-focused ∪
direct children of focused roots`. The footer's
`sessions.length - subagents.length` arithmetic still produces the
root count.

`liveSessions()` now returns the union of focuses across all live
clients (was: the keys of the per-session refcount map).

Subscriptions without `X-Client-ID` are unchanged — they get the same
event stream and do not contribute to liveness.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
